# Q57 (the author; next_core_tasks_v2.md K03): an unknown head inside a definition defines a NESTED named Structure --
# `C: makeA()` with both names unknown is C holding an empty named makeA (a field of kind 2, as the `(): name`
# spelling declares one), and the block form `D:` / `E:` / `end:` is the same resolution with fields: D\E\x reads 5.
# Was "internal: an own declaration has no physical field": makeA fell through to a statement of C's procedure and
# then to an own row without a slot.  Success is 7.
C: makeA()
D:
    E:
        size_t: x 5U
    end: E
end: D
fn: check () int
    size_t: v
    v: D\E\x
    if: v != 5U
        return: 1
return: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
